/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  layoutDict -- the PLOT PLAN and the GMP INTERIOR of the donepezil tablet
  plant (DEV.md 4c C104, C110).  A STARTING POINT for the group, to copy and
  change.

  WHAT STANDS WHERE, AND WHY.  An oral-solid-dose plant is a building
  before it is a plot plan: every process item stands in a ROOM of the
  `building {}` at the end of this file (each room's `equipment ( ... )`
  lists it; its base is the room's floor, so no item indoors declares a
  `z`):
    * the binder-solution tank, in the GRANULATION room beside the
      high-shear granulator it feeds;
    * the coating-suspension tank, in a COATING-PREPARATION room beside the
      coater;
    * the two air heaters -- the fluid bed's and the coater's -- in the
      air-handling plant on the technical floor, above the rooms they serve.
  NOTHING STANDS OUTDOORS.  Unlike apalutamide01_tablets there is no
  organic solvent, so there is no tank farm, no pipe rack, no bund and no
  hazardous area anywhere on this site: purified water is made in the
  building (its plant is not modelled), the air is drawn from outside, and
  every powder arrives in drums or bags through the warehouse.  Beside the
  production building stand the site buildings as NON-PROCESS items: the
  offices and quality-control laboratory by the main gate, the warehouse,
  and a second (emergency) gate on the north side.

  WHAT IS THE ENGINE'S AND WHAT IS OURS.  The two tanks' diameters and
  heights are their sizers' own; the air heaters publish an AREA, not a
  shape, so their plan boxes are DECLARED below (each with the arithmetic).
  EVERYTHING ELSE IS AN AUTHOR-SET ASSUMPTION FOR THE GROUP TO REPLACE WITH
  ITS OWN SITE DATA: every position, every building's size, every road and
  the access distance.  They are round numbers, not values from any spacing
  or fire standard (the published ones grant no redistribution, and a
  citation invented for a round number would turn "unsourced" into
  "falsely sourced").

  PIPES INDOORS ARE NOT DRAWN.  The router draws pipes in the open only: a
  stream whose ends stand indoors is listed as "inside the building: indoor
  piping is not routed"; the two purified-water feeds and the two air
  intakes come from supplies this case does not model and are listed with
  that reason; SOLIDS ARE NOT PIPED -- the powders, the wet mass, the
  granules, the blend and the tablets are listed as "solids only, moved in
  containers or by conveyor".  See the README (section 7).

  Grammar and checks: docs/design/a-plant-layout-is-declared-and-checked.md
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

